Z||000008||ray b||06-22-2001||06:52 PM||||manual valve body is dragrace trick only will shift on lever move [auto manual]lets you rev it way up, and shift at or over red line. don't know if itis made for 125 trans or if can be adapted to it from another gm unit.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000009||theogre||06-22-2001||08:21 PM||||manual shifting for an automatic is usually a rework of the existing valve body. Very similar to installing a shift kit. I would not recomend these on street use cars. They are really only made for drag cars.<P>Shift kits mainly rework the valve body to change shift timing. I've found with TH125 that a slight tweek of the TV cable usually has similar results. <P>Overall, on any stock Fiero I don't think I'd use one. If you think you are loosing power the first things to check are what final gears are in it and the adjustment of the TV cable.<P>Condition of fluid is also important. Simply changing the fluid to DexronIII can help allot more than you'd think. I was very pleased with the fluid change results on my car. I've done fluid before but DexronIII is a real improvement.<P>You have to get out as much old fluid as you can. the method I use is in my cave but not everyone is comfortable with that.<P>Before you do put ont in,,, you have to be sure the tranny is good. The kit could hide some defects or even agravate others.||||reg||1
