Z||000011||pHoOl||06-22-2001||11:36 PM||||This gets back to the age old discussion of, if you manually shift your auto (without doing any fancy reworks just hand and lever)  does it drain life of the trans?  Some say yes, some say no.  I would tend to think that from what i've heard in this discussion that it would be fine for the tranny, since you'd be giving it harder shifts, therefore wearing the clutch out less.  However, my father the engineer (hi dad!!) would tell me that an automatic transmission was designed to be put in drive and that's it.  <P>So which is it?<P>------------------<BR>Ricers are like tampons... Every p@#%y has one.<P>AIM: phool88fiero<P>      <IMG SRC="http://www.gvsuphool.homestead.com/files/phoolsig1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000012||Fierowrecker||06-23-2001||01:47 AM||||Don't be a fool Phool!<BR>Sorry, couldn't resist...<P>You should go with a heavy duty shift kit for better shifting without the whiplash effect...<BR>But if you want the best performance, go with the performance shift kit...<BR>I had many mods done to my turbo 400 back when I drag raced...<BR>The only thing that took away from streetabillity was the stall converter...<BR>I raced and drove on the street for 10 years, and all I did was change tranny fluid every spring...<BR>I blew out 3 differentials and 2 drive shafts, but the tranny held up without a hiccup...<BR>crash...||||reg||1
